      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <p class="lede">
          Menopause speeds up the loss of muscle and bone, and protein, alongside strength training, is one of the few things you control that pushes back. The best protein powder for menopause gives you 25-30 g of protein and roughly 2.5-3 g of leucine in a single serving, because that is the dose older muscle needs to respond. Transparent Labs Grass-Fed Whey Isolate is our top pick, with 28 g of protein per scoop and independent testing per the brand. Momentous is the NSF certified option, NOW Sports Soy Isolate is the best soy choice, and Naked Casein is the evening pick. Soy isoflavones are not a reliable hot-flash treatment, and no protein powder replaces calcium, vitamin D or medical care. This guide is not medical advice.
        </p>

        <QuickPicks products={PRODUCTS} />

        <div id="at-a-glance" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. Menopause Protein Powders Compared at a Glance
          </h2>

          <p>
            Here is every pick side by side. Protein, calories and sugar are per serving from the label or retailer listings at the time of writing and vary by flavor. Price tier compares cost per serving across this list.
          </p>

