              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  The RDA is 0.8 g per kilogram a day, but expert groups such as PROT-AGE recommend 1.0-1.2 g per kilogram for adults over 65, and many dietitians apply a similar range from menopause onward. Aim for about 25-30 g at each meal. Talk to your doctor before increasing protein if you have kidney disease.
