                  Possibly a little, but the evidence is inconsistent. Some meta-analyses found isoflavone supplements reduced hot flashes modestly, while a Cochrane review found no conclusive benefit, and The Menopause Society does not recommend soy for hot flashes. Soy protein powders rarely list isoflavone content. Soy is a good protein for muscle, but treat any symptom relief as a bonus.
                </p>
