            <details class="faq-item">
              <summary><h3>Is whey or soy better for menopause?</h3></summary>
              <div class="faq-answer">
                <p>
                  For muscle, whey has the edge because it contains more leucine per gram, so a smaller serving reaches the per-meal threshold. Soy is a complete protein and works well if you eat a slightly bigger serving, about 30 g or more. Choose soy if you avoid dairy or like soy foods, and whey if you want the most efficient dose.
                </p>
